in. Based on its ability to function as both a cyclooxygenase and as a peroxidase, the encoded protein has been identified as a moonlighting protein. The protein may promote cell proliferation during tumor progression. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Nov 2021]"}], "gene_ontology":{"assigned_by":"GOA", "molecular_functions":[{"name":"heme binding", "go_id":"GO:0020037", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"oxidoreductase activity, acting on paired donors, with incorporation or reduction of molecular oxygen", "go_id":"GO:0016705", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"oxidoreductase activity, acting on single donors with incorporation of molecular oxygen, incorporation of two atoms of oxygen", "go_id":"GO:0016702", "evidence_code":"IBA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"peroxidase activity", "go_id":"GO:0004601", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"prostaglandin-endoperoxide synthase activity", "go_id":"GO:0004666", "evidence_code":"IBA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"prostaglandin-endoperoxide synthase activity", "go_id":"GO:0004666", "evidence_code":"IDA", "qualifier":"enables", "reference":{"pmids":["1380156"]}}, {"name":"prostaglandin-endoperoxide synthase activity", "go_id":"GO:0004666", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"enables"}, {"name":"protein binding", "go_id":"GO:0005515", "evidence_code":"IPI", "qualifier":"enables", "reference":{"pmids":["32814053"]}}], "biological_processes":[{"name":"cellular oxidant detoxification", "go_id":"GO:0098869", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"involved_in"}, {"name":"cyclooxygenase pathway", "go_id":"GO:0019371", "evidence_code":"IBA", "qualifier":"involved_in"}, {"name":"cyclooxygenase pathway", "go_id":"GO:0019371", "evidence_code":"IDA", "qualifier":"involved_in", "reference":{"pmids":["1380156"]}}, {"name":"cyclooxygenase pathway", "go_id":"GO:0019371", "evidence_code":"IEA", "qualifier":"involved_in"}, {"n